From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:16:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] SensorManager JNI: include <arpa/inet.h> for htonl

toUint64 calls htonl, which the file gets only through bionic headers
including <netinet/in.h> transitively (sys/endian.h). POSIX declares
htonl in <arpa/inet.h>; glibc headers have no such transitive include.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: the file relies on a bionic-only transitive include; the glibc header shape cannot add it (a sys/endian.h -> netinet/in.h row fails the compile-alone check) and a redeclaration of htonl clashes with glibc's noexcept one
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 core/jni/android_hardware_SensorManager.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/core/jni/android_hardware_SensorManager.cpp b/core/jni/android_hardware_SensorManager.cpp
index 2864a5718f338a1fe0727a06d21b807bc1c8e2d3..c06fb104a9cc635c402827c5940b2b478348d7aa 100644
--- a/core/jni/android_hardware_SensorManager.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/android_hardware_SensorManager.cpp
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include <utils/Looper.h>
 #include <utils/Vector.h>
 
+#include <arpa/inet.h>
 #include <map>
 
 namespace {
